%N A401880 a(n) is the number of distinct placements of two nonoverlapping congruent Pythagorean triangles whose acute angles meet to form a right angle at a corner of an n X n square.
%C A401880 The objective is to form a complete right angle at a single corner of an n X n square using two non-overlapping, congruent Pythagorean triangles. Their complementary acute angles must meet at that corner and together form 90 degrees; merely touching the corner is insufficient. Both triangles must lie entirely within the square, with one side of each triangle along a different adjacent side of the square. Placing triangles at separate corners or using a triangle's right angle at the chosen corner is not permitted. Empty space elsewhere is allowed. Distinct configurations are counted up to reflections, according to the side lengths and orientations of the triangles forming the corner.
%C A401880 For each Pythagorean triple (a,b,c) with a < b < c, it contributes 1 placement if b <= n < c and 4 placements if c <= n.
%H A401880 Janaka Rodrigo, <a href="/A401880/b401880.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..500</a>
%H A401880 Janaka Rodrigo, <a href="/A401880/a401880.txt">Python Code</a>
%F A401880 a(n) = Sum_{k=1..n} 3*A046080(k) + A056137(k).
%e A401880 n = 8 has 5 distinct placements; 4 from the triple (3,4,5) and 1 from the triple (6,8,10). Therefore a(8) = 5.
%Y A401880 Cf. A400884, A046080, A056137.
%K A401880 nonn,new
%O A401880 1,5
%A A401880 _Janaka Rodrigo_, Nov 08 2026
